Package: SpatialCopyInference
Title: Spatial Copy Number Inference from Xenium Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Floris", "Honig", , "florishonig@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: SpatialCopyInference infers chromosome arm-level somatic copy number aberrations
    (SCNAs) directly from Xenium spatial transcriptomics data. The package
    identifies and spatially maps SCNA-defined cell populations through
    spatial clustering and provides downstream tools for visualisation,
    differential expression analysis, pathway enrichment and identification
    of genes and genomic regions associated with inferred SCNAs.
    SpatialCopyInference enables the study of tumour evolution and early
    cancer development in situ.
